Defend cleaning without losing the manufactured function (@cm-study-microclean: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Cleaning-Technology-in-Semiconductor-Device-Manufacturing-VIII.lingua#r_1CVF9XCJR7E3J37X5150BDS5Y2", #source "../sources/Particle-Removal-and-MEMS-Damage-Hirano.lingua#r_0RH4K2MTZZG42NZ4MMZE1K6G9E", #clean-manufacturing "Review-cleaning-before-designing-the-facility-and-its-controls.lingua#r_1GWH14SX8FEJ49VV0SN0XDAM06") { r_188DKZBJJETJFPKYH27SH91AQE
**Read:** [Cleaning technology in semiconductor device manufacturing VIII — ECS proceedings](../sources/Cleaning-Technology-in-Semiconductor-Device-Manufacturing-VIII.lingua#r_1CVF9XCJR7E3J37X5150BDS5Y2), complete particle-removal, microstructure, post-CMP and material-compatibility articles chosen for the comparison; [Particle removal and MEMS damage — Hirano and colleagues](../sources/Particle-Removal-and-MEMS-Damage-Hirano.lingua#r_0RH4K2MTZZG42NZ4MMZE1K6G9E) as a second research system.

Compare at least two cleaning mechanisms for a declared substrate, residue and vulnerable feature. Track chemical changes, removal, redeposition and damage independently. Interpret the measurement's spatial resolution and count model before ranking efficiencies.

**Work:** Reconstruct a primary result, including initial state, controls, detection, sampled geometry and uncertainty. Recompute the occupancy example and explain when its correction is appropriate. Develop a process window supported by both removal and retained function, then test how that conclusion changes with one material or feature-size assumption. Historical papers supply evidence within their conditions; extend to a newer process only with new relevant evidence.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
**Continue in clean manufacturing:** [Review cleaning before designing the facility and its controls](Review-cleaning-before-designing-the-facility-and-its-controls.lingua#r_1GWH14SX8FEJ49VV0SN0XDAM06).

